Selected button and tracking sprites are retained from the upstream asset
bundle: Capture (JailButton), Mark, Recall, Alert, Shoot (SheriffShootButton),
Arrow, and Beacon0–Beacon9 (EscapistMark_0–EscapistMark_9).
Role/button/options registration, meeting cleanup, Reactor RPC transport,
Mira custom murder/game-over integration, task counting, critical-sabotage
checks, and revive/presentation patterns were adapted and simplified from
Town of Us Mira and MiraAPI. This plugin does not include or link against
TownOfUsMira.dll. Role mechanics, host validation, UI, and presentation have
been substantially modified for AmongUsDogsRoles's ten-role roster.

Explode, Sniff, Execute, Release, Investigate, ChainLink, Fake, Unfake,
Blast0–Blast35 and Explosion.wav are original artwork/audio under this
mod's GPL-3.0 license. Their editable sources and generators are included.

Runtime dependencies retain their own licenses:
MiraAPI: https://github.com/All-Of-Us-Mods/MiraAPI
Reactor: https://github.com/NuclearPowered/Reactor
BepInEx: https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx
The release loader also includes Doorstop, Il2CppInterop, and .NET;
its license notices and upstream source/reference archives are bundled
with the release. Unmodified loader files originate from the Town of Us
Mira 1.7.3 Windows distribution.

Among Us and its game assets belong to Innersloth. Users supply their own
installed copy. This is an unofficial mod, not an Innersloth product.

Optional development tools: Reactor.Debugger, NuclearPowered and contributors,
LGPL-3.0-or-later, Reactor 2.5.1 commit
04100970b66d57a2dd96f6f4eae0383362e9a321. setup-testing.ps1 downloads its
source separately. The test helper adapts its dummy-spawning approach;
the helper's remaining panel and test-state code is new and uses GPL-3.0.
Neither testing plugin is part of the production mod.

